  "2026-09-19T16:37:09.203Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: all-status keyword searches for jscpd and jscpd 5.3 found the closed 5.2 owner pm-qs5iiq and no 5.3 upgrade owner; open and in-progress inventories inspected. Registry jscpd 5.3.0 was published 2026-09-18T12:55:38.703Z and supports Node >=18. No runtime-floor change or release-age override is authorized or needed."
  "2026-09-19T16:46:04.585Z","harness:codex","Normal pnpm update selected jscpd 5.3.0 and platform binaries without release-age exclusions. pnpm audit reports zero vulnerabilities across 364 dependencies. Other available major upgrades remain with canonical live owners pm-fokyhh (CodSpeed lacks Vitest 5 peer support), pm-do5b (TypeScript 7 compiler API and typescript-eslint peer boundary), pm-ksr40d (npm-package-arg 14 raises the supported Node floor); no duplicate upgrade items created."
  "2026-09-19T16:50:32.308Z","harness:codex","Release checks independently verified: scheduled Auto Release run 35429507172 and exact-tag publish run 35430412823 succeeded today; v2026.9.19 is public and non-draft. The automatic workflow first checks an existing UTC-day tag and verifies/reuses its exact publication instead of creating another automatic release. New branch changes remain for the next eligible daily release. No release mutation or same-day override performed."
  "2026-09-19T17:03:07.280Z","harness:codex","Final scoped verification: all three clone profiles pass with jscpd 5.3.0; the real historical low-token table-clone negative control rejects duplication and accepts its shared declaration. Frozen-lockfile reinstall and audit pass. Graph composition now reports pass with discovery provenance linking the inspected major-upgrade owners, verifies edges to both decomposition items, and parent quality lineage; record integrity also passes."
